        {
          "path": "_m/9/w/0/m/jerome-arizona-wp/jerome-arizona-45858250834.jpg",
          "filename": "Jerome, Arizona (45858250834).jpg",
          "caption": "Jerome, Arizona was founded in the late 19th century on Cleopatra Hill overlooking the Verde Valley. It exists because of mining, mainly copper but also gold, silver and other minerals and elements.\nThe quarries and mines are large and several underground shafts were made around and under the town. As a consequence subsidence destroyed several of Jerome's buildings, which slid slowly downhill during the first half of the 20th century - including the jail and the post office. Notice also, the building on the right of my photo.\nMining came to a halt in the 1950's and the town's population dropped to almost nothing. Concerted efforts were made to revitalise the town by getting it designated as a National Historic Landmark and then attracting tourists - which appears to have succeeded well. \n\nI found it to be a quirky, fascinating place and hope to revisit.",
          "alt": "Jerome, Arizona was founded in the late 19th century on Cleopatra Hill overlooking the Verde Valley. It exists because of mining, mainly copper but also gold, silver and other minerals and elements.\nThe quarries and mines are large and several underground shafts were made around and under the town. As a consequence subsidence destroyed several of Jerome's buildings, which slid slowly downhill during the first half of the 20th century - including the jail and the post office. Notice also, the building on the right of my photo.\nMining came to a halt in the 1950's and the town's population dropped to almost nothing. Concerted efforts were made to revitalise the town by getting it designated as a National Historic Landmark and then attracting tourists - which appears to have succeeded well. \n\nI found it to be a quirky, fascinating place and hope to revisit.",
          "width": 8549,
          "height": 4497,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "Mike McBey",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jerome,_Arizona_(45858250834).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "jerome-arizona-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "9w0m",
          "accessedAt": "2026-02-21T23:31:12.169Z",
          "smallPath": "_m/9/w/0/m/jerome-arizona-wp/jerome-arizona-45858250834-small.jpg",
          "mediumPath": "_m/9/w/0/m/jerome-arizona-wp/jerome-arizona-45858250834-medium.jpg"
        },
        {
          "path": "_m/9/w/0/m/jerome-arizona-wp/jerome-arizona-27544564988.jpg",
          "filename": "Jerome Arizona (27544564988).jpg",
          "caption": "Jerome, to me, is a fascinating place with a great \"vibe\".\nLocated on State Route 89A between Sedona and Prescott it's history is completely linked to mining. \nHuge deposits of ore bearing mainly copper, but also gold &amp; silver were mined here from 1883 until 1953, when the ore deposits ran out and the mines closed.  As a result of the extensive underground mining, parts of the town have slid down the hill and several buildings were lost that way. After the mines closed the population dwindled to fewer than 100. \n\nIn recent times the town has re-invented itself as  a tourist attraction and is a National Historic Landmark.",
          "alt": "Jerome, to me, is a fascinating place with a great \"vibe\".\nLocated on State Route 89A between Sedona and Prescott it's history is completely linked to mining. \nHuge deposits of ore bearing mainly copper, but also gold &amp; silver were mined here from 1883 until 1953, when the ore deposits ran out and the mines closed.  As a result of the extensive underground mining, parts of the town have slid down the hill and several buildings were lost that way. After the mines closed the population dwindled to fewer than 100. \n\nIn recent times the town has re-invented itself as  a tourist attraction and is a National Historic Landmark.",
          "width": 4435,
          "height": 2169,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "Mike McBey",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jerome_Arizona_(27544564988).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "jerome-arizona-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "9w0m",
          "accessedAt": "2026-02-21T23:31:12.169Z",
          "smallPath": "_m/9/w/0/m/jerome-arizona-wp/jerome-arizona-27544564988-small.jpg",
          "mediumPath": "_m/9/w/0/m/jerome-arizona-wp/jerome-arizona-27544564988-medium.jpg"
        },
        {
          "path": "_m/9/w/0/m/jerome-arizona-wp/moonbow-over-jerome-at-night-2.jpg",
          "filename": "Moonbow Over Jerome at Night 2 (7927669020).jpg",
          "caption": "A rainbow was created by a full moon rising directly behind me as I took this shot.  Sometimes referred to as a \"moonbow,\" this is a rare occurrence given the number of variables that have to be just right for one to form.  This moonbow rose over the historic Arizona mining town of Jerome.",
